From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ryan Murray <ryan@aurorasilicon.org>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 12:09:29 +1100
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: cs42l84: Range-check DAC volume values before narrowing
 them

cs42l84_put_dac_vol() adds mc->min to the user's long values and checks
the int results. A value far outside the control's range can wrap into
range when it is narrowed. Commit eaefdaa73035 ("ASoC: cs42l84: honour
the platform volume limit") then compares the original long against
platform_max, and a large negative value passes that test as well, so
the write can still set the DAC above the machine driver's ceiling.

Check both values as longs against 0..max-min first, as
soc_mixer_valid_ctl() does for the stock volsw handlers.

Fixes: eaefdaa73035 ("ASoC: cs42l84: honour the platform volume limit")
Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Ryan Murray <ryan@aurorasilicon.org>
(cherry picked from commit 40350fad7ae96dcddbd63ade6bc4e0ccc52cfe9e)
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
---
 sound/soc/codecs/cs42l84.c | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/sound/soc/codecs/cs42l84.c b/sound/soc/codecs/cs42l84.c
index c210a5c400..85e5027f19 100644
--- a/sound/soc/codecs/cs42l84.c
+++ b/sound/soc/codecs/cs42l84.c
@@ -93,9 +93,15 @@ static int cs42l84_put_dac_vol(struct snd_kcontrol *kctl,
 {
 	struct snd_soc_component *component = snd_kcontrol_chip(kctl);
 	struct soc_mixer_control *mc = (struct soc_mixer_control *) kctl->private_value;
+	long range = mc->max - mc->min;
 	int vola, volb;
 	int ret, ret2, updated = 0;
 
+	/* Check the user values as longs, before they are narrowed to int. */
+	if (val->value.integer.value[0] < 0 || val->value.integer.value[0] > range ||
+	    val->value.integer.value[1] < 0 || val->value.integer.value[1] > range)
+		return -EINVAL;
+
 	vola = val->value.integer.value[0] + mc->min;
 	volb = val->value.integer.value[1] + mc->min;
 
